a coined term is a debt the reader pays at every use. spend it only
where the trade has no word. server-side validation, payload key, error
code, entry point — the trade's. the door, the floor, the exit — ours,
and ours cost a lookup to everyone who did not sit in the room.

define at first use, beside the mechanism it stands for. a glossary
below the prose that needed it arrives after the reader is already lost.

the test: hand it to someone who knows the trade and not this tree.
every word they stop on is either defined above the line they stopped
on, or was the wrong word.

`general/reader` decides which words those are. `general/figures` is the
same debt taken out in pictures instead of names.
